        <body>
            <div xml:id="d305">

                <pb facs="0517" n="405" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg405"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 2338/11.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Ambassador White</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-02-28"><hi rendition="#italic">February 28,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to previous instructions relative
                    to American salted meats in France, the department incloses herewith copy of a
                    letter from Messrs. Armour &amp; Co., of Chicago, Ill., dated the 18th
                    instant.</p>
                <p>The department will be pleased to receive from you a report relative to the
                    status of the question of admission of American salted meats into France when
                    accompanied by the certificates of inspection contemplated by our
                    meat-inspection law of June 30, 1906.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Elihu Root.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d305-a1.xml" xpointer="d305-a1"/>
            </div>
